# Screenshot apps like iShot capture "the window under the pointer" on its own: they list the
# screen's windows front to back and take the first ordinary one at the point. Over a page that
# was a clear window laid over it, the status bubble's page-sized panel or the empty Chromium
# window whose page had moved into the card, so the shot came out blank white (GitHub #346).
# Anywhere over the page outside the bubble's strip the pick is the main window, which draws
# the page in its card; the bubble's panel is only its strip at the page's bottom left.
# promise: #346
budget rss=700 stalls50=5
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=screenshot
wait 2
# The page area spans x 328…1190 from y 10 (debugger-infobar), the strip its bottom left.
cra://debug?screenshotPick=760,400
expect-log screenshot pick at 760,400: main window
cra://debug?screenshotPick=1100,780
expect-log screenshot pick at 1100,780: main window
cra://debug?screenshotPick=340,780
expect-log screenshot pick at 340,780: window [0-9]+ 540x34
reject-log fault:
